Name: aurora-voice-speech
Source: plugins/voice/speech.py
Copy-Of: plugins/voice/speech.py
Summary: Aurora's speech client, copied verbatim from the voice plugin.

There is one voice in Aurora and this is it. A plugin that speaks does not write its
own client for the speech service, pick its own model, or decide on its own what to
do when a key is missing — all three were different here until this copy replaced
them, and two implementations of the same request to the same host are two places
for an answer to come back wrong.

It is a copy rather than an import because plugins do not share a process, a
sandbox, or a directory: each one is granted its own, and nothing outside it is
readable. The copy is checked byte for byte by test_vendored_speech, which fails
the build if the two drift apart.

Do not edit this file. Edit plugins/voice/speech.py and copy it here:

    cp plugins/voice/speech.py plugins/discord/vendor/aurora_voice/speech.py
